{:answer/id #uuid "8f2a67da-c228-5676-a777-e1b1a6c13d87" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{3}+5{x}^{2}+x-75" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186609484} {:answer/id #uuid "cee5b84d-afb0-56a0-ba99-96c4ec3716b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{3}+{x}^{2}-8x-25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186609595} {:answer/id #uuid "f4f28660-87ee-5d8a-9f01-9de3d9bf769c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}+26" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186609667}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8f2a67da-c228-5676-a777-e1b1a6c13d87" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{3}+5{x}^{2}+x-75" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186609484} :answer-field/id #uuid "baa03b9d-33f3-5d43-b148-3d0455ebddcc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186609780}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "aa8bd427-119e-5635-9eee-cca9530d1d5c" :question/math-academy-id "q-17406" :question/problem "![](images/7b/7b0db4e1a1d7cfcc94a4e91329a51e05d9266ceec9c5bf0f08fac1abb7755dca.png)\n\nThe Argand diagram above shows the roots of a cubic polynomial $f(x).$\nFind $f(x)$ given that the coefficient of the cubic term is $1.$" :question/worked-solution "From the diagram, we see that $f(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}=3$ and ${x}_{2,3}=-4\\pm 3\\text{i}.$ Additionally, we're given that the coefficient of the cubic term is $a=1.$ Therefore, we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3}) \\\\  & =1(x-3)(x-(-4+3\\text{i}))(x-(-4-3\\text{i})) \\\\  & =(x-3)(x-(-4+3\\text{i}))(x-(-4-3\\text{i}))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-3)(x-(-4+3\\text{i}))(x-(-4-3\\text{i})) & = \\\\ (x-3)({x}^{2}-x(-4-3\\text{i})-x(-4+3\\text{i})+(-4+3\\text{i})(-4-3\\text{i})) & = \\\\ (x-3)({x}^{2}+8x+25) & = \\\\ {x}^{3}+8{x}^{2}+25x-3{x}^{2}-24x-75 & = \\\\ {x}^{3}+5{x}^{2}+x-75 & .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)={x}^{3}+5{x}^{2}+x-75.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186609895 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a09f413-b43c-5cc6-a386-11a6bfa67f18" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{x}^{3}-8{x}^{2}+40x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186609296} {:answer/id #uuid "39635b11-d427-50e5-9b6b-35f0a5b475a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{x}^{3}-8{x}^{2}+10x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186609327} {:answer/id #uuid "c5a2dc8d-c85a-583d-b4e5-9da4f3446751" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{x}^{3}+8{x}^{2}+10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186609571} {:answer/id #uuid "dbf018d5-087f-5e80-90fc-e8eee5f0060d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{x}^{3}-8x+10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186609613} {:answer/id #uuid "eb50c3b7-0901-57ae-bf8c-c6de6e21bb56" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{x}^{3}+8{x}^{2}-40x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186609650}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2a09f413-b43c-5cc6-a386-11a6bfa67f18" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{x}^{3}-8{x}^{2}+40x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186609296} :answer-field/id #uuid "156b0c91-6d3c-5c38-8300-996e23fd491d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186609698}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "db01e234-0926-5c05-b215-68219b2a79a6" :question/math-academy-id "q-104483" :question/problem "The cubic polynomial $f(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}=0,{x}_{2,3}=1\\pm 3\\text{i},$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $4.$ Find $f(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Since $f(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}=0$ and ${x}_{2,3}=1\\pm 3\\text{i},$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $a=4,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3}) \\\\  & =4(x-0)(x-(1+3\\text{i}))(x-(1-3\\text{i})) \\\\  & =4x(x-(1+3\\text{i}))(x-(1-3\\text{i}))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x(x-(1+3\\text{i}))(x-(1-3\\text{i})) & = \\\\ 4x({x}^{2}-x(1-3\\text{i})-x(1+3\\text{i})+(1+3\\text{i})(1-3\\text{i})) & = \\\\ 4x({x}^{2}-2x+10) & = \\\\ 4{x}^{3}-8{x}^{2}+40x & .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)=4{x}^{3}-8{x}^{2}+40x.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186610922 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04a648ed-f9e5-58b6-9b46-11fbdf23fab2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "w=\\frac{1}{3},\\,\\pm 2\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186610546} {:answer/id #uuid "8a6306e8-3399-5157-bb83-18a001ab017d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "w=2,\\,\\pm 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186610701} {:answer/id #uuid "9ee0b5e7-23f9-54f3-b5fb-c7db51252165" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "w=\\frac{1}{3},\\,\\pm 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186610722} {:answer/id #uuid "ab7e1972-7c78-5e02-800c-544511931f6a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "w=3,\\,\\pm 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186610739} {:answer/id #uuid "d2b8c1d9-a53b-5ee6-b3e2-48f968baf811" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "w=3,\\,\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{1}{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186610782}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "04a648ed-f9e5-58b6-9b46-11fbdf23fab2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "w=\\frac{1}{3},\\,\\pm 2\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186610546} :answer-field/id #uuid "9d0d7d8f-6dac-50ea-9833-6bc94037807f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186610882}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "27efb0fd-42e9-58ec-b0d2-666ee0ad363a" :question/math-academy-id "q-114214" :question/problem "Solve $-3{w}^{3}+{w}^{2}+24w-8=0.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we multiply the equation by $-1$ to make the coefficient of the cubic term positive. This gives\n\n$$\n3{w}^{3}-{w}^{2}-24w+8=0.\n$$\n\nWe then proceed to factor the left-hand side by grouping:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{w}^{3}-{w}^{2}-24w+8 & = \\\\ (3{w}^{3}-{w}^{2})+(-24w+8) & = \\\\ {w}^{2}(3w-1)-8(3w-1) & = \\\\ ({w}^{2}-8)(3w-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we solve $({w}^{2}-8)(3w-1)=0$ by setting each factor equal to $0.$\n\n- Setting the factor $({w}^{2}-8)$ equal to $0,$ we get $w=\\pm 2\\sqrt{2}.$\n\n- Setting the factor $(3w-1)$ equal to $0,$ we get $w=\\frac{1}{3}.$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $w=\\frac{1}{3},\\,\\pm 2\\sqrt{2}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186612419 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "63d04367-3ee6-5ce4-8b40-c6e61e1653e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186611911}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "63d04367-3ee6-5ce4-8b40-c6e61e1653e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186611911} :answer-field/id #uuid "1a05f9f9-3b8e-5b2c-8d90-13c5009840ef" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186612264} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ac6b4759-2c8f-59b8-a2cb-9fe43e1965ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186612064}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ac6b4759-2c8f-59b8-a2cb-9fe43e1965ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186612064} :answer-field/id #uuid "61970d22-7e5b-5922-9664-71734e1d8f9d" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186612306}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2d47cddb-62a1-5595-bd01-6be1d75265a7" :question/math-academy-id "q-175524" :question/problem "$\\frac{11}{9}y+8+\\frac{16}{9}y+3=${{field-1}}\n$y\\,+$\n{{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "We collect and combine the like terms, simplifying the coefficients as much as possible:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{11}{9}y+8+\\frac{16}{9}y+3 & = \\\\ (\\frac{11}{9}y+\\frac{16}{9}y)+(8+3) & = \\\\ (\\frac{11}{9}+\\frac{16}{9})y+11 & = \\\\ (\\frac{11+16}{9})y+11 & = \\\\ \\frac{27}{9}y+11 & = \\\\ 3\\,y+11\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186612423 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2ea2af0c-afde-56a9-943e-d4f847688779" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x+6y+5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186611804} {:answer/id #uuid "3b54dfcb-570e-5aab-9baa-0c3ed28bee72" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x+8y-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186611832} {:answer/id #uuid "53cb55ab-00fa-55bb-89d4-a3200f47464d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x+4y-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186611874} {:answer/id #uuid "7fe54ba1-b4a0-51a4-9e4e-facedb693b17" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x+8y+6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186611967} {:answer/id #uuid "ef2fee30-c104-5851-a2e8-7dee88d2ee13" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x+4y-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186612211}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3b54dfcb-570e-5aab-9baa-0c3ed28bee72" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x+8y-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186611832} :answer-field/id #uuid "90ddf786-e8b9-5ddd-9ff8-429b8b28e39c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186612336}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "32a1c383-5ee7-5c00-a341-d8977cc8f73a" :question/math-academy-id "q-2309" :question/problem "$\\frac{1}{2}(4x+16y-12)+2=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we apply the distributive law:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}(4x+16y-12)+2 & = \\\\ (\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 4)x+(\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 16)y-(\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 12)+2 & = \\\\ (\\frac{4}{2})x+(\\frac{16}{2})y-(\\frac{12}{2})+2 & = \\\\ 2x+8y-6+2\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we collect and combine the like terms, simplifying the coefficients as much as possible:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}2x+8y-6+2 & = \\\\ 2x+8y+(-6+2) & = \\\\ 2x+8y-4\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186612426 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "669a2bb6-b68c-595d-808e-cd3d07020776" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186611916}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "669a2bb6-b68c-595d-808e-cd3d07020776" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186611916} :answer-field/id #uuid "520b398b-7625-53df-a501-9af72546f850" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-fie