 (-\\frac{y}{4}) & = \\\\ \\frac{12x}{3}+(-\\frac{12y}{4}) & = \\\\ 4\\,x-3\\,y & \\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186612493 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3a21c2a6-bab5-5202-a490-cc59fb68d1be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2u}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186611824} {:answer/id #uuid "4569dd4c-6b59-5a97-81d8-d66efb412b31" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7u}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186611847} {:answer/id #uuid "9913f763-77ae-59b3-8bc6-cdfcea9c66a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{u}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186612022} {:answer/id #uuid "bd230f7c-5dad-5105-ac9a-bd7183f9bd71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186612098} {:answer/id #uuid "def58d4e-59c9-5aab-9a08-bee1010ae14d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4u}{15}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186612171}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4569dd4c-6b59-5a97-81d8-d66efb412b31" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7u}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186611847} :answer-field/id #uuid "fc086df5-f359-5b84-bba9-23c16142acd5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186612400}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f866fd89-a627-5ee7-a95a-055fcfea22aa" :question/math-academy-id "q-51658" :question/problem "$\\frac{u}{4}+\\frac{u}{3}=$" :question/worked-solution "We combine the like terms by adding the coefficients:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{u}{4}+\\frac{u}{3} & = \\\\ (\\frac{1}{4}+\\frac{1}{3})u\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn order to add the coefficients, we have to convert them to have the same denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\frac{1}{4}+\\frac{1}{3})u & = \\\\ (\\frac{3}{12}+\\frac{4}{12})u & = \\\\ (\\frac{3+4}{12})u & = \\\\ (\\frac{7}{12})u & = \\\\ \\frac{7u}{12}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186612494 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a0d3fe4-10d9-536c-a5f9-12ffe9c7e64f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{11}b-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186611732} {:answer/id #uuid "61a1db79-ad50-5f1f-8d3f-56b7153d0017" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{11}b" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186611905} {:answer/id #uuid "887ff158-fe80-5186-ac13-c2c2b71618cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{11}b-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186611986} {:answer/id #uuid "b703941b-c9df-5af2-8f01-490935932a81" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{11}b+2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186612080} {:answer/id #uuid "ea2bc32f-0db4-518f-8b4f-48890b0e42e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{11}b-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186612200}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "887ff158-fe80-5186-ac13-c2c2b71618cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{11}b-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186611986} :answer-field/id #uuid "2131822e-8291-56db-acb7-551feee7cbe9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186612270}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "fa1c3b13-d6b5-52ef-8d51-0fe7d3f37a7d" :question/math-academy-id "q-51441" :question/problem "$12-\\frac{3}{11}b-14+\\frac{4}{11}b=$" :question/worked-solution "We collect and combine the like terms, simplifying the coefficients as much as possible:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}12-\\frac{3}{11}b-14+\\frac{4}{11}b & = \\\\ (-\\frac{3}{11}b+\\frac{4}{11}b)+(12-14) & = \\\\ (\\frac{-3+4}{11})b-2 & = \\\\ \\frac{1}{11}b-2\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186613148 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5e67c85a-e22f-57c0-91d1-9febf218f28a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2{x}^{2}-x-1}}{x-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186612750} {:answer/id #uuid "6a64e606-1f5c-5ebd-84ae-374a30912ada" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2{x}^{2}-x-1}}{x+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186612769} {:answer/id #uuid "71486130-2163-5f0c-b8d8-c0eb0b17e854" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{x-1}}{x-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186612783} {:answer/id #uuid "87113b08-2a4c-5c71-8f76-9893b066651f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2{x}^{2}+x-1}}{x+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186612828} {:answer/id #uuid "8aa56882-d002-5fd1-b99b-eb792427e630" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2{x}^{2}+x-1}}{x-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186612833}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5e67c85a-e22f-57c0-91d1-9febf218f28a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2{x}^{2}-x-1}}{x-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186612750} :answer-field/id #uuid "5e7f5b87-33c9-5d22-b3f5-f9fe41aae505" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186613059}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "42d9b0f9-f882-5332-9f6a-ff5014f429dc" :question/math-academy-id "q-365108" :question/problem "Express $\\frac{\\sqrt{2x+1}}{\\sqrt{x-1}}\\,$ without radicals in the denominator." :question/worked-solution "To remove the radical $\\sqrt{x-1}$ from the denominator, we multiply both the numerator and denominator by $\\sqrt{x-1}$ and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\sqrt{2x+1}}{\\sqrt{x-1}} & = \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{2x+1}}{\\sqrt{x-1}}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{x-1}}{\\sqrt{x-1}} & = \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{2x+1}\\cdot \\sqrt{x-1}}{(\\sqrt{x-1})^{2}} & = \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{(2x+1)(x-1)}}{x-1} & = \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{2{x}^{2}-x-1}}{x-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186613189 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6bf50515-0204-578b-aeae-fc99d02e6c7f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186612771} {:answer/id #uuid "84120683-155f-5780-96e8-45cf67f3b679" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7m}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186612821} {:answer/id #uuid "93dd27ec-f681-5bf8-8fb7-a9102e70b95c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186612847} {:answer/id #uuid "ac0d5a16-d190-56bf-8c3a-6c9513a08422" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7m}{5m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186612882} {:answer/id #uuid "d20d0f54-a159-54d3-a73b-88685541ad0f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5m}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186612937}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "93dd27ec-f681-5bf8-8fb7-a9102e70b95c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186612847} :answer-field/id #uuid "90b731ca-ed67-5026-a7eb-38f1af6bed7a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186613079}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b5f413f7-cb9b-5844-93ec-c729504a345e" :question/math-academy-id "q-3640" :question/problem "$\\frac{m+5}{7}÷\\frac{{m}^{2}+5m}{5m}=$" :question/worked-solution "To compute\n\n$$\n\\frac{m+5}{7}÷\\frac{{m}^{2}+5m}{5m},\n$$\n\nwe just need to multiply by the reciprocal of the divisor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{m+5}{7}÷\\frac{{m}^{2}+5m}{5m} & = \\\\ \\frac{m+5}{7}\\cdot \\frac{5m}{{m}^{2}+5m} & = \\\\ \\frac{m+5}{7}\\cdot \\frac{5m}{m(m+5)} & = \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{m+5}}{7}\\cdot \\frac{5\\cancel{m}}{\\cancel{m}\\cancel{(m+5)}} & = \\\\ \\frac{5}{7}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186613740 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "137314c7-c9ad-5b9a-b808-d0b932499932" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6.2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186613320} {:answer/id #uuid "3f63c005-74dc-57f5-b913-b2f5f84f5872" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13.1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186613374} {:answer/id #uuid "56fbb167-21c0-5e09-9b3d-2504c5d166c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10.3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186613413} {:answer/id #uuid "6b398c35-fce1-5e91-9940-19ecfa9ef4ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12.4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186613447} {:answer/id #uuid "94d46aa0-a977-5800-9036-15dde227b59b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14.2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186613493}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6b398c35-fce1-5e91-9940-19ecfa9ef4ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12.4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186613447} :answer-field/id #uuid "68a4f65d-cfd1-52cb-aa72-7ee305082b98" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186613666}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1448b8af-0cec-5e40-87ce-912c8dc4bd2e" :question/math-academy-id "q-99737" :question/problem "A cricketer has played $5$ matches in a month and his scores in those matches are:\n\n$$\n43,\\,31,\\,72,\\,51,\\,63\n$$\n\nRounded to one decimal place, what is the mean absolute deviation of the cricketers' scores?" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the mean of the data:\n\n$$\n\\text{mean}=\\frac{43+31+72+51+63}{5}=\\frac{260}{5}=52\n$$\n\nNext, we subtract the mean from each number in the data set, find the absolute value of the results, and add all these together:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|43-52|+|31-52|+|72-52|+|51-52|+|63-52| & = \\\\ |\\,-9\\,|+|-21|+|\\,20\\,|+|\\,-1\\,|+|\\,11\\,| & = \\\\ 9+21+20+1+11 & = \\\\ 62 & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to calculate the mean absolute deviation (MAD), we divide the sum obtained above ($62$) by the total number of data points ($5$):\n\n$$\n\\text{MAD}=\\frac{62}{5}=12.4\n$$\n\nTherefore,  the mean absolute deviation of the cricketer's scores is $12.4.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186613744 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7734b40c-a840-5663-9ff0-c59f8e9ca10a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186613456}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7734b40c-a840-5663-9ff0-c59f8e9ca10a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186613456} :answer-field/id #uuid "b2e96dda-6e41-53dc-9d95-3d26c34bddb9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186613697}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "21682148-d08a-5a39-8f5a-172a76270306" :question/math-academy-id "q-235807" :question/problem "$$\n8,\\,6,\\,6,\\,10,\\,5\n$$\n\nThe mean absolute deviation of the data set above is{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we find the mean of the data:\n\n$$\n\\text{mean}=\\frac{8+6+6+10+5}{5}=\\frac{35}{5}=7\n$$\n\nNext, we subtract the mean from each number in the data set, find the absolute value of the results, and add all these together:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|8-7|+|6-7|+|6-7|+|10-7|+|5-7| & = \\\\ |\\,1\\,|+|-1|+|\\,-1\\,|+|\\,3\\,|+|\\,-2\\,| & = \\\\ 1+1+1+3+2 & = \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to calculate the mean absolute deviation (MAD), we divide the sum obtained above ($8$) by the total number of data points ($5$):\n\n$$\n\\text{MAD}=\\frac{8}{5}=1.6\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186613749 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "48506b01-da1b-5c6b-8adc-af09132f18e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186613388} {:answer/id #uuid "926a5468-0528-57b7-bb34-5c156cb884a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186613489} {:answer/id #uuid "af71a956-6aba-547e-b47d-9dd39b3b63ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186613528} {:answer/id #uuid "cb8e2399-113d-51ce-97b5-9ff9cb1e28b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186613574} {:answer/id #uuid "f0c2d89a-ed3a-5d62-a62a-05d48573bff7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186613613}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "48506b01-da1b-5c6b-8adc-af09132f18e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186613388} :answer-field/id #uuid "706c5fc5-353f-5b5f-8034-6b31fed66982" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186613672}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "30c7ae58-a160-5224-b937-3d255e08d18c" :question/math-academy-id "q-62656" :question/problem "Given that the mean of the data set below is $5$, what is the mean absolute deviation of the data?\n\n$$\n3,\\,4,\\,6,\\,8,\\,4\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Since we are given the mean ($5$), we subtract it from each number in the data set, find the absolute value of the results, and add all these together:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|3-5|+|4-5|+|6-5|+|8-5|+|4-5| & = \\\\ |-2|+|-1|+|\\,1\\,|+|\\,3\\,|+|-1| & = \\\\ 2+1+1+3+1 & = \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to calculate the mean absolute deviation (MAD), we divide the sum obtained above ($8$) by the total number of data points ($5$):\n\n$$\n\\text{MAD}=\\frac{8}{5}=1.6\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186613763 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "383db465-b01e-5a28-9ad4-6c9f0aa63a4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186613370} {:answer/id #uuid "42a7e190-98c7-5c03-8672-176ad7570c2f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186613380} {:answer/id #uuid "a139a52b-1c47-51ed-b076-844cf6f8cafe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186613512} {:answer/id #uuid "c3c6d849-e1b8-5caf-954b-aab529ae2856" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186613564} {:answer/id #uuid "f89a631c-4036-5769-b519-f994f70c5da3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186613618}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f89a631c-4036-5769-b519-f994f70c5da3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186613618} :answer-field/id #uuid "adb1009f-2f61-5a30-ae54-06c83ab557ab" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186613692}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5340ed07-6c7b-57cb-91ef-d48e696e1834" :question/math-academy-id "q-160584" :question/problem "The shoe sizes of four friends are as follows:\n\n$$\n36,\\,37,\\,37,\\,38\n$$\n\nWhat is the mean absolute deviation of the friends' shoe sizes?" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the mean of the data:\n\n$$\n\\text{mean}=\\frac{36+37+37+38}{4}=\\frac{148}{4}=37\n$$\n\nNext, we subtract the mean from each number in the data set, find the absolute value of the results, and add all these together:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|36-37|+|37-37|+|37-37|+|38-37| & = \\\\ |-1|+|0|+|\\,0\\,|+|\\,1\\,| & = \\\\ 1+0+0+1 & = \\\\ 2 & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to calculate the mean absolute deviation (MAD), we divide the sum obtained above ($2$) by the total number of data points ($4$):\n\n$$\n\\text{MAD}=\\frac{2}{4}=0.5\n$$\n\nTherefore,  the mean absolute deviation of the friends' shoe sizes is $0.5.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186613765 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "25294cad-3f88-5f8f-bfb2-34b8de21cbe3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186613347}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "25294cad-3f88-5f8f-bfb2-34b8de21cbe3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186613347} :answer-field/id #uuid "d411ca56-7777-584f-9794-29d6d44206f2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186613711}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "541c1f26-be92-50d3-8627-218e9b251876" :question/math-academy-id "q-235478" :question/problem "$$\n7,\\,6,\\,9,\\,4\n$$\n\nGiven that the mean of the data set above is $6.5$, the mean absolute deviation of the data is{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Since we are given the mean ($6.5$), we subtract it from each number in the data set, find the absolute value of the results, and add all these together:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|7-6.5|+|6-6.5|+|9-6.5|+|4-6.5| & = \\\\ |0.5|+|-0.5|+|\\,2.5\\,|+|-2.5| & = \\\\ 0.5+0.5+2.5+2.5 & = \\\\ 6 & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to calculate the mean absolute deviation (MAD), we divide the sum obtained above ($6$) by the total number of data points ($4$):\n\n$$\n\\text{MAD}=\\frac{6}{4}=1.5\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186613770 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0245f147-be5d-5cf3-af7f-3f237302b2a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.4\\,\\text{kg}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186613298} {:answer/id #uuid "52ffdf38-440c-5429-a8c0-e17a42a2a208" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.4\\,\\text{kg}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186613409} {:answer/id #uuid "7279dea6-c592-5df5-b596-a28195e8ae09" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.8\\,\\text{kg}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186613452} {:answer/id #uuid "e97234a0-cea9-5648-adb6-03090064642c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/valu