#edb/ref 17592186613773 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "19dd7ab5-c6a1-5bc7-afad-dabd8977a730" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.4\\,\\text{oz}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186613329} {:answer/id #uuid "2aba2bef-bc3b-5263-af8c-bfd9d73bdfd1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.8\\,\\text{oz}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186613353} {:answer/id #uuid "4031f4f7-aabd-56bc-8340-d98ce3bbbfc0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.2\\,\\text{oz}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186613377} {:answer/id #uuid "a7333345-fe13-57b8-898d-98e538ee861e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.5\\,\\text{oz}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186613518} {:answer/id #uuid "ecdf5957-a107-5bab-a151-211f00a9425f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.6\\,\\text{oz}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186613609}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4031f4f7-aabd-56bc-8340-d98ce3bbbfc0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.2\\,\\text{oz}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186613377} :answer-field/id #uuid "1566826f-86cd-5fb3-bb17-d16cb422963f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186613639}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6bfa9467-8f27-59b8-a0fb-1e5979ff24d4" :question/math-academy-id "q-160592" :question/problem "A basket has five fruits whose weights are as follows:\n\n$$\n7\\,\\text{oz},\\,5\\,\\text{oz},\\,4.5\\,\\text{oz},\\,6\\,\\text{oz},\\,2.5\\,\\text{oz}\n$$\n\nWhat is the mean absolute deviation of the fruits' weights?" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the mean of the data:\n\n$$\n\\text{mean}=\\frac{7+5+4.5+6+2.5}{5}=\\frac{25}{5}=5\n$$\n\nNext, we subtract the mean from each number in the data set, find the absolute value of the results, and add all these together:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|7-5|+|5-5|+|4.5-5|+|6-5|+|2.5-5| & = \\\\ |\\,2\\,|+|0|+|\\,-0.5\\,|+|\\,1\\,|+|-2.5| & = \\\\ 2+0+0.5+1+2.5 & = \\\\ 6 & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to calculate the mean absolute deviation (MAD), we divide the sum obtained above ($6$) by the total number of data points ($5$):\n\n$$\n\\text{MAD}=\\frac{6}{5}=1.2\n$$\n\nTherefore,  the mean absolute deviation of the fruits' weights is $1.2\\,\\text{oz}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186613776 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "206484df-e7f5-5d3b-9dcc-6a0076cf3e60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$15$ dollars" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186613340} {:answer/id #uuid "3975e2ad-cb61-5232-8052-5c7dbf37a17b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$13$ dollars" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186613372} {:answer/id #uuid "561c78fd-d0b1-51ae-b5f4-642f78c5bb81" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$10$ dollars" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186613412} {:answer/id #uuid "96090df9-8d52-50a7-a9c0-82dcb3b29acc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$12.50$ dollars" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186613495} {:answer/id #uuid "fb3e5a84-14bd-550e-9ba1-b838958d48fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$7.70$ dollars" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186613624}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3975e2ad-cb61-5232-8052-5c7dbf37a17b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$13$ dollars" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186613372} :answer-field/id #uuid "208529f2-de8a-5814-b172-d7806f4c54c4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186613642}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "81279681-9066-509a-8f14-599fc783ee17" :question/math-academy-id "q-160586" :question/problem "Tom has six dollar bills in his pocket of the following denominations:\n\n$$\n1\\,\\text{dollar},\\,1\\,\\text{dollar},\\,10\\,\\text{dollars},\\,20\\,\\text{dollars},\\,20\\,\\text{dollars},\\,50\\,\\text{dollars}\n$$\n\nWhat is the mean absolute deviation of Tom's dollar bills?" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the mean of the data:\n\n$$\n\\text{mean}=\\frac{1+1+10+20+20+50}{6}=\\frac{102}{6}=17\n$$\n\nNext, we subtract the mean from each number in the data set, find the absolute value of the results, and add all these together:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|1-17|+|1-17|+|10-17|+|20-17|+|20-17|+|50-17| & = \\\\ |-16|+|-16|+|-7|+|\\,3\\,|+|\\,3\\,|+|\\,33\\,| & = \\\\ 16+16+7+3+3+33 & = \\\\ 78 & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to calculate the mean absolute deviation (MAD), we divide the sum obtained above ($78$) by the total number of data points ($6$):\n\n$$\n\\text{MAD}=\\frac{78}{6}=13\n$$\n\nTherefore,  the mean absolute deviation of Tom's dollar bills is $13$ dollars."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186613782 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "26c21812-e5f7-5e8c-afba-332578febcd5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186613348} {:answer/id #uuid "2db0ea5f-b7be-5461-9a36-368e1910095c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186613360} {:answer/id #uuid "491c3092-78ec-5602-b7cd-06dbafaed774" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186613391} {:answer/id #uuid "69aa80be-6674-5d32-8b0f-8e059205ff34" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 1