), we divide the sum obtained above ($4$) by the total number of data points ($4$):\n\n$$\n\\text{MAD}=\\frac{4}{4}=1\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186613795 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c46dd8c-7be0-583c-a2d5-a848260590dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186613314}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0c46dd8c-7be0-583c-a2d5-a848260590dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186613314} :answer-field/id #uuid "b084133b-54b4-563b-bdf5-d77687ed5583" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186613694}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "bf496653-725f-57e0-bda4-ad77d63c62cd" :question/math-academy-id "q-235475" :question/problem "$$\n6,\\,3,\\,5,\\,1,\\,5\n$$\n\nGiven that the mean of the data set above is $4$, the mean absolute deviation of the data is\n\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Since we are given the mean ($4$), we subtract it from each number in the data set, find the absolute value of the results, and add all these together:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|6-4|+|3-4|+|5-4|+|1-4|+|5-4| & = \\\\ |2|+|\\,-1\\,|+|1|+|\\,-3\\,|+|1| & = \\\\ 2+1+1+3+1 & = \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to calculate the mean absolute deviation (MAD), we divide the sum obtained above ($8$) by the total number of data points ($5$):\n\n$$\n\\text{MAD}=\\frac{8}{5}=1.6\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186613796 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15147248-163b-5e82-a467-ba021c87fb3e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186613322} {:answer/id #uuid "23b180ab-2b53-56c4-adee-5eba5e3ad12f" :answer/type {:db/id #